# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quizzle — environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values from your Firebase project:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# This file is committed on purpose and must contain PLACEHOLDERS ONLY.
# Never put real credentials in it. `.env` and all `.env.*` variants are
# gitignored, so real values stay on your machine.
#
# Only variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ are exposed to the client bundle.
# Anything secret (AI provider keys, service-account JSON) must NEVER go here —
# it belongs in the server-side API layer, which is not yet implemented.
#
# Restart the Expo dev server after editing `.env`; the values are inlined at
# build time and are not hot-reloaded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Firebase: REQUIRED for Google sign-in ---------------------------------

# Firebase Console -> Project settings -> General -> Your apps -> SDK setup and
# configuration -> Config  (these are the `firebaseConfig` values)
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-web-api-key
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project-id.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000

# --- Firebase: recommended -------------------------------------------------

# Needed later for Firestore-adjacent features and Cloud Messaging.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.appspot.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000

# --- Firebase: optional ----------------------------------------------------

# Only if you enable Google Analytics for Firebase.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-0000000000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY NOTE — read before adding anything else here
#
# The values above are Firebase *web* config, which is public by design: it is
# shipped in the client bundle of every Firebase web app and is not a secret.
# They identify your project; they do not grant access to it.
#
# Access is controlled by, in order of importance:
#   1. Firestore security rules (must be deployed — see docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md)
#   2. Firebase Auth: the Authorized Domains allowlist
#   3. App Check (recommended, later)
#
# Therefore: NEVER put an AI provider key, a Firebase service-account key, or
# any server secret in this file. Those belong in the server-side API layer,
# which is deliberately not implemented yet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
